Elements of Mechanical Design — MIT 2.72, Spring 2009 (@mech-mit-design: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mech-sources) { r_31S9Z88TMF2875BF5KA5825GX7
Martin Culpepper. [MIT OpenCourseWare course](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-72-elements-of-mechanical-design-spring-2009/) · [Lecture notes](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-72-elements-of-mechanical-design-spring-2009/pages/lecture-notes/).

An advanced undergraduate design course with public notes, assignments, labs and a desktop-lathe project. Follow the complete available sequence during the machine-element and integrated-design work. It gives a substantial example of joining analysis, fabrication and characterization; it does not supply a beginner's entire mechanics education.

The course, lecture index and selected shaft, bearing, flexure, bolted-joint, screw, gear, actuator and friction-element PDFs were inspected on 30 October 2026. The screw-drive file is an eight-page activity outline, with some images removed; Slocum supplies a fuller derivation. The historical friction-element notes include obsolete materials, which are not recommendations for a new design. Sessions 15 and 17 list topics without attached lecture PDFs; project sessions also differ from supplied notes. Do not call the topic list a complete recorded course. OCW's CC BY-NC-SA terms and separately credited notices apply. Commercial readings mentioned by the course retain their own access conditions. A published project description is not evidence that a reader has constructed or tested its machine.

**Return:** [Mechanical-engineering sources](../Sources.lingua#r_06RZYPZEFNMZ6MZ690QB1WN1Z2).
